{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b4de9903-5575-403e-b3e4-02e0bc41aa31","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b431386b9d98dd33","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-vtpt3q_y/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Per-project Kueue quota data exposure for chargeback reporting\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Distributed Workloads side of consumption-against-quota reporting: per-project Kueue quota data, surfaced in a form the administrator-facing chargeback reporting can consume. It covers the quota half of the requirement that the administrator view show current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota; the consumption (GPU-hour) half is delivered by the metering strategy and the reporting work built on it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Surface each project's Kueue quota (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) as per-project quota data consumable by the administrator reporting view, via a stable, documented contract.\n- Determine and implement the exposure mechanism over the platform's existing Distributed Workloads interfaces (Kueue CRs and/or the existing Kueue metrics exposure) — the specific mechanism is the owning team's decision.\n- Document the consumption contract for the Dashboard integration: data shape, per-project mapping, and refresh characteristics.\n- Contingency: if existing Kueue surfaces (CRs/metrics) already provide the needed per-project quota data without code changes, this epic's deliverable collapses to defining, validating, and documenting that contract rather than new exposure code.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Per-project Kueue quota data for every project that holds quota is retrievable by the administrator reporting view through the documented contract.\n- The exposed quota data correctly reflects the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model as shipped by the platform (verified against live CRs).\n- The consumption contract (data shape, per-project mapping, refresh characteristics) is documented for the Dashboard integration.\n- Existing Distributed Workloads build pipelines remain green with the changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1) — quota data side: the Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota; this epic supplies the quota data that view is compared against.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50798,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b7fef0fecbadf42","agent_id":"a7d7cb158c442f48e","session_id":"2d213be9-f60a-4255-a607-da491d2b37a9","uuid":"15d35a70-dbba-46f0-9ea7-b8845802bc33","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:24:13.382Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
