{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-46998f94-bf99-49ca-831a-266a4d2d2dba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1c82cfb4704493a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-vtpt3q_y/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# GPU chargeback report computation, CSV export, and reporting API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the backend of administrator chargeback reporting: computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), plus export of those reports as CSV and retrieval via a stable API for finance tooling. It consumes the metering data; it must not re-implement collection.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over administrator-selectable time ranges, sourced from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy.\n- Export the computed reports as CSV.\n- Expose the computed reports through a stable API suitable for finance tooling integration, with a documented API contract.\n- Expose the reporting capability behind the Dashboard's existing per-component feature-flag mechanism so it can be enabled/disabled per deployment.\n- Resolve the hosting placement of the reporting API and computation against the Dashboard's architectural constraint that it exposes no private component APIs — the placement decision belongs to the implementing team and must be recorded.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Per-project GPU-hour consumption reports are computable over selectable time ranges and return correct per-project totals for the selected range.\n- Reports are computed exclusively from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy; no metering collection logic is re-implemented (verified by review: no collection path added).\n- Reports are exportable as C