 and refresh characteristics.\n40\t- Contingency: if existing Kueue surfaces (CRs/metrics) already provide the needed per-project quota data without code changes, this epic's deliverable collapses to defining, validating, and documenting that contract rather than new exposure code.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Per-project Kueue quota data for every project that holds quota is retrievable by the administrator reporting view through the documented contract.\n45\t- The exposed quota data correctly reflects the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model as shipped by the platform (verified against live CRs).\n46\t- The consumption contract (data shape, per-project mapping, refresh characteristics) is documented for the Dashboard integration.\n47\t- Existing Distributed Workloads build pipelines remain green with the changes.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-3 (P1) — quota data side: the Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota; this epic supplies the quota data that view is compared against.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2091d34576a6f9e","agent_id":"aa99bb01dbbce016e","session_id":"2d213be9-f60a-4255-a607-da491d2b37a9","uuid":"52055c38-ecdf-4b57-ac53-d11c600c78ea","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:25:55.683Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad4b04fc6ca2375a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
