a data contract; it adds no parallel data plumbing.\n43\t- Follow the Dashboard's existing view/navigation conventions for the new administrator section, including feature-flag gating inherited from the reporting capability.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- An administrator can select a time range and see per-project GPU-hour consumption for that range in the Dashboard admin view.\n48\t- The admin view shows each project's current-month consumption against its Kueue quota.\n49\t- The view is visible only to users holding the administrator role; non-administrator users cannot access it.\n50\t- All report and quota data rendered in the view is served through the reporting API and the documented quota data contract.\n51\t- Existing Dashboard build pipelines remain green with the changes.\n52\t\n53\t## Risks / Notes\n54\t\n55\t- Indirect external timing risk: the consumption data this view renders is computed from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990); the view is ready to execute once the reporting API it consumes is available.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-1 (P0) — view side: administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges.\n60\t- HLR-3 (P1, bundled) — the Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota. Bundled with HLR-1's view because the quota comparison is a panel of the same administrator report view over the same consumption data; splitting it would fragment one UI surface and duplicate the view plumbing.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2091d34576a6f9e","agent_id":"aa99bb01dbbce016e","session_id":"2d213be9-f60a-4255-a607-da491d2b37a9","uuid":"ac85263d-dd67-432a-9acf-e9ed0914b120","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:25:59.040Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8ea94ecc4f866b7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpos